course: dictionary
lesson: 1582
title: Words in brackets: chastity
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some writers explain a hard word straight after they use it, inside brackets. These brackets are context clues, and they do the work for you. «Monks and nuns live in communities devoted to prayer and service, with vows of poverty (owning nothing of their own), chastity (not marrying) and obedience (doing as their leaders say).»
explain: Chastity is the middle one of three promises. The brackets say chastity means not marrying, so a vow of chastity is a promise to choose not to marry. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "vows of poverty, not marrying and obedience" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Chastity is a formal church word. You will meet it in religion lessons and in old stories about being good and pure. Because it is formal, it does not appear in everyday talk, so check the words around it.
fact: Chastity means not having a sexual relationship, or only within marriage, as a religious or moral choice.
fact: Chastity is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say "chastity", not "a chastity".
fact: In church life, chastity is one of three vows, with poverty and obedience.
fact: Formally, «chastity» can also mean being pure and simple in style, without anything fussy or extra.
fact: Context clues such as brackets, commas and examples can explain a hard word right next to it.
exercise: In the sentence «vows of poverty (owning nothing of their own), chastity (not marrying) and obedience», what does chastity mean? | Praying every day | Doing as your leaders say | *Not marrying, as a religious promise | Owning nothing of your own
exercise: Which vow means owning nothing of your own? | *Poverty | Chastity | Service | Obedience
exercise: Find and copy the word that means doing as your leaders say. | prayer | *obedience | chastity | communities
test: Monks and nuns make three vows. Which vow is about not marrying? | Service | Poverty | Obedience | *Chastity
test: Which sentence uses chastity correctly? | *The nun kept her vow of chastity. | The chastity ran quickly across the field. | Chastity is a very tall and green tree.
exam: Which is the best explanation of chastity from the brackets in «chastity (not marrying)»? | *Not marrying, as part of a religious promise | Praying in a community | Doing as your leaders say | Owning nothing of your own
